  "variation": {
    "seeded": true,
    "notes": "Every meteor's size, approach and landing spot (scatter_px) change per cast, so the storm never lands the same way twice; the two big meteors always land near the centre. The rhythm of the falls is fixed: seven rocks over about two seconds."
  },
  "director_notes": "From Lisa's spells01 image, Sorcerer - Meteor Storm: 'fire falls from the heavens'. The existing Meteor Strike is one rock; this is the area version. Seven orb meteors on staggered travel beats, each with scatter_px (new) so it lands somewhere on the field, and the impact sparks, rubble, crater and burn of each are attach_to that meteor (new for sparks and decals) so they appear where it lands. Two bigger meteors land near the centre for weight. A dark cloud deck and a red sky glow sit at the sky anchor; a fire field and embers cover the footprint."
}
